#: ../src/genkey.c:28
#, fuzzy, c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Usage: %s gen_key [OPTIONS]... EMAIL\n"
#| "\n"
#| "Generate an OpenPGP key pair (public and secret) according to PGP ID standards.\n"
#| "Output 3 lines for each fingerprints:\n"
#| "* main key (Sign Certify)\n"
#| "* decryption key (Encrypt)\n"
#| "* authentication key (Auth)\n"
#| "\n"
#| "OPTIONS:\n"
#| "  -N, --name PSEUDONYM             Common name or pseudonym. Default: first part of email\n"
#| "  -c, --eid U4|U5                  Entity ID. Worldwide and decentralised entity identifier. Required here\n"
#| "  -C, --extra-comment NOTE         Supplemental information or comment associated with the entity\n"
#| "  -p, --passphrase PASSPHRASE      Passphrase to (symetric) encrypt secret part of OpenPGP key. CAN'T BE EMPTY (at this stage)\n"
#| "  -P, --passfrom FILE              Get passphrase from first line of FILE (eg: fifo, tmpfs, /dev/stdin …)\n"
#| "  -e, --expiration YEARS           Number of years before certificate expiration. Default: 11\n"
#| "  -k, --keyserver KEYSERVER        Prefered OpenPGP certificate server. Default: %s\n"
#| "  -h, --help                       Print this help and exit\n"
#| "  -V, --version                    Print the version and exit\n"
#| "\n"
#| "Both ways of giving the passphrase have their drawback, and the second has\n"
#| "fewer: an argument is visible to every process on the machine for as long\n"
#| "as this one runs.\n"
msgid ""
"Usage: %s gen_key [OPTIONS]... EMAIL\n"
"\n"
"Generate a PGP key pair (public and secret) according to PGP ID standards.\n"
"Output 3 lines for each fingerprints:\n"
"* main key (Sign Certify)\n"
"* decryption key (Encrypt)\n"
"* authentication key (Auth)\n"
"\n"
"OPTIONS:\n"
"  -N, --name PSEUDONYM             Common name or pseudonym. Default: first part of email\n"
"  -c, --eid U4|U5                  Entity ID. Worldwide and decentralised entity identifier. Required here\n"
"  -C, --extra-comment NOTE         Supplemental information or comment associated with the entity\n"
"  -p, --passphrase PASSPHRASE      Passphrase to (symetric) encrypt secret part of PGP key. CAN'T BE EMPTY (at this stage)\n"
"  -P, --passfrom FILE              Get passphrase from first line of FILE (eg: fifo, tmpfs, /dev/stdin …)\n"
"  -e, --expiration YEARS           Number of years before certificate expiration. Default: 11\n"
"  -k, --keyserver KEYSERVER        Prefered PGP certificate server. Default: %s\n"
"  -h, --help                       Print this help and exit\n"
"  -V, --version                    Print the version and exit\n"
"\n"
"Both ways of giving the passphrase have their drawback, and the second has\n"
"fewer: an argument is visible to every process on the machine for as long\n"
"as this one runs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usage: %s gen_key [OPTIONS]... ADRES\n"
"\n"
"Wytworzyć parę kluczy OpenPGP (jawny i tajny) wedle norm PGP ID.\n"
"Wypisuje 3 wiersze, po jednym na odcisk:\n"
"* klucz główny (Podpis Poświadczenie)\n"
"* klucz deszyfrujący (Szyfrowanie)\n"
"* klucz uwierzytelniający (Auth)\n"
"\n"
"OPTIONS:\n"
"  -N, --name PSEUDONYM        Nazwa zwyczajowa lub pseudonim\n"
"  -c, --eid U4|U5             Identyfikator jednostki. Wymagany: wyliczenie\n"
"  -C, --extra-comment NOTE    Notatka o jednostce\n"
"  -p, --passphrase PASSPHRASE Fraza. Widoczna dla wszystkiego, co potrafi\n"
"  -P, --passfrom FILE         Odczytać ją z pierwszego wiersza PLIKU\n"
"  -e, --expiration YEARS      Lata do wygaśnięcia - Domyślnie: 11\n"
"  -k, --keyserver KEYSERVER   Serwer, który ten certyfikat zwie swoim - Domyślnie: %s\n"
"  -h, --help                  Wypisać tę pomoc i zakończyć\n"
"  -V, --version               Wypisać wersję i zakończyć\n"
"\n"
"Oba sposoby podania hasła mają swoją wadę, a drugi mniejszą: argument jest\n"
"widoczny dla każdego procesu na maszynie, dopóki ten trwa.\n"

