#: ../src/get.c:27
#, fuzzy, c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Usage: %s get [OPTIONS]... NAME|U4|U5|EMAIL...\n"
#| "\n"
#| "Output fingerprints, emails and eid of certificates matching NAME|U4|U5|EMAIL.\n"
#| "May also get or refresh certificates from keyservers.\n"
#| "'*' matches the whole keyring; `list` is the one that shows everything\n"
#| "when asked nothing.\n"
#| "\n"
#| "OPTIONS:\n"
#| "  -F, --fingerprint           Output only fingerprints\n"
#| "  -E, --email                 Output only emails\n"
#| "  -f, --no-fetch              Don't refresh certificates from keyservers or Web Key Directories\n"
#| "  -m, --errexit-g=1           Return an error if there is more than one (1) entry - You may replace '1' by an other number\n"
#| "  -K, --keyservers KEYSERVERS Search and refresh certificates from this keyservers - Default: %s\n"
#| "  -h, --help                  Print this help and exit\n"
#| "  -V, --version               Print the version and exit\n"
#| "\n"
#| "There is no 'cert_check': `list` answers what it answered, for less.\n"
msgid ""
"Usage: %s cert_get [OPTIONS]... NAME|U4|U5|EMAIL...\n"
"\n"
"Output fingerprints, emails and eid of certificates matching NAME|U4|U5|EMAIL.\n"
"May also get or refresh certificates from keyservers.\n"
"'*' matches the whole keyring; `list` is the one that shows everything\n"
"when asked nothing.\n"
"\n"
"OPTIONS:\n"
"  -F, --fingerprint           Output only fingerprints\n"
"  -E, --email                 Output only emails\n"
"  -f, --no-fetch              Don't refresh certificates from keyservers or Web Key Directories\n"
"      --import-from FILE      Take the certificate from a file rather than a keyserver\n"
"  -r, --recurse[=NUM]         Also fetch the certificates signing the target, NUM\n"
"                              levels deep (0..6) - Default with -r: 1\n"
"  -m, --errexit-g=1           Return an error if there is more than one (1) entry - You may replace '1' by an other number\n"
"  -K, --keyservers KEYSERVERS Search and refresh certificates from this keyservers - Default: %s\n"
"  -h, --help                  Print this help and exit\n"
"  -V, --version               Print the version and exit\n"
"\n"
"There is no 'cert_check': `list` answers what it answered, for less.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usage: %s get [OPTIONS]... NAZWA|U4|U5|ADRES...\n"
"\n"
"Wypisuje odciski, adresy i eid certyfikatów pasujących do\n"
"NAZWA|U4|U5|ADRES.\n"
"Może też pobrać lub odświeżyć certyfikaty z serwerów kluczy.\n"
"'*' znaczy cały pęk; `list` jest tą, która pokazuje wszystko, gdy się jej o\n"
"nic nie pyta.\n"
"\n"
"OPTIONS:\n"
"  -F, --fingerprint           Wypisać tylko odciski palca\n"
"  -E, --email                 Wypisać tylko adresy\n"
"  -f, --no-fetch              Nie odświeżać z serwerów kluczy ani z WKD\n"
"  -m, --errexit-g=1           Zawieść, jeśli pasuje więcej niż N certyfikatów\n"
"  -K, --keyservers KEYSERVERS Odświeżyć z tych, rozdzielonych spacjami - Domyślnie: %s\n"
"  -h, --help                  Wypisać tę pomoc i zakończyć\n"
"  -V, --version               Wypisać wersję i zakończyć\n"
"\n"
"Nie ma „cert_check”: `list` odpowiada to, co odpowiadał, mniejszym kosztem.\n"
"\n"

